WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.320
- Hi, my name is Jacob
Scott Thomas Bertrand,

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.260
and I play Hawk.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:05.600
- Hi, I am Mary Mouser, and
I play Samantha LaRusso.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.693
- Hey, I'm Peyton List, and I play Tory.

00:00:07.693 --> 00:00:08.526
- Hi, I'm Xolo Maridueña,

00:00:08.526 --> 00:00:10.640
and I play Miguel Diaz from Cobra Kai.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.040
Today we are with Buzzfeed to take a quiz

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.247
to find out if we're more
Cobra Kai or Miyagi-Do.

00:00:16.247 --> 00:00:20.260
(cool mid tempo music)

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.550
First, choose the word
that best describes you.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.950
Our options are: loyal,

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:26.890
kind,

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.030
supportive,

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:29.870
brave, ambitious,

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.150
and reliable.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.240
I think, right off the bat,

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.600
I'm gonna have to go
with ambitious, I think.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.420
I wouldn't consider myself brave.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.060
I can cross that one
right off off the bat.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.580
What about you guys? What
are you guys thinking?

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:40.650
- I think supportive.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.840
I mean, I wanna say loyal.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:43.700
Definitely not reliable.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.250
I'm late to everything.
(Xolo laughs)

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:48.060
Don't invite me anywhere, I
might not show up, I'm terrible.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.230
But supportive, I feel like I could do.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.710
- I'm thinking supportive too.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:55.460
- I would probably say brave.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.790
I was gonna do ambitious, but-
- You can just say

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:58.900
that I have the best answers,

00:00:58.900 --> 00:00:59.880
it's not a problem Jacob.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.309
- [Mary] Now pick your biggest weakness.

00:01:02.309 --> 00:01:04.364
- This is going to get so
personal for all of us.

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:05.416
(Mary laughs)

00:01:05.416 --> 00:01:06.690
- And we all just start crying, right?

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:09.509
I get too emotionally attached?

00:01:09.509 --> 00:01:11.850
(Jacob laughs)
I'm done, that's all I needed.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.860
- I feel like this is a little targeted.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.060
(Jacob laughs)
- I know, right?

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:16.190
I'm really insecure.

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:19.720
Ooh, (giggles) I'm a little selfish.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.360
I trust too easily.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.800
I'm kind of stubborn.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.370
I'm a bit bossy.

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:25.882
- Can I only choose one?

00:01:25.882 --> 00:01:27.679
(laughing)

00:01:27.679 --> 00:01:28.650
- Can I get multiple choice?

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:31.180
To be fair, I feel like
insecurity definitely is

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.700
the thing that holds me back,

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.870
but boy, do I ever trust too easily?

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:37.130
I'm also stubborn as hell.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.290
I mean, all right.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:40.000
I'm just going to go with insecure,

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.610
because, let's be honest.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:43.040
- I get too emotionally attached,

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.120
or I trust too easily.
- I went with stubborn.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.300
- Yeah, you're stubborn as (beep)

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:47.880
- I wanna say I trust too easily.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.650
- I think I'm stubborn.

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:52.962
- Yeah, we all think so too.
- Yeah. (laughs)

00:01:52.962 --> 00:01:56.420
- Peyton, I'm so glad I don't
have to work with these two

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.520
all the time like you do.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.060
(Mary and Jacob laugh)
- The feeling's mutual,

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.344
don't worry.

00:02:01.344 --> 00:02:02.250
- Choose a Cobra Kai character

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:03.826
you'd trust with a secret:

00:02:03.826 --> 00:02:07.760
Pam, Miguel, Hawk,
Tori, Ayesha, or Robbie.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.850
And I would have to go with Ayesha,

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:12.280
because I feel like she
was a great friend to Tori,

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:14.120
and I also feel like
she's super trustworthy

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.370
and I would trust her the most.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.820
- I feel like there's so many bad answers.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:21.780
I love Hawk, but no way in hell

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.837
would I tell that man anything.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:26.700
Honestly, I would totally say Miguel.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:27.533
- That's true.

00:02:27.533 --> 00:02:28.460
- I'm gonna go with Robbie.

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:29.293
I trust Robbie.

00:02:29.293 --> 00:02:31.880
I trust that Robbie has no one to tell.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:32.980
- I chose myself.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:35.897
There's no one that I can trust
better than myself, right?

00:02:35.897 --> 00:02:37.940
You can't trust nobody out here.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:39.400
Everyone's kissing each other,

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.500
and everyone's going
behind each other's backs

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:42.370
and backstabbing,

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:43.700
I can only trust myself.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.720
- [Jacob] Choose a bad-ass
fictional character

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:46.940
to fight alongside:

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:49.620
Wonder Woman, Katniss Everdeen
from "The Hunger Games",

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.320
Adonis Creed from "Creed",

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.600
John McClane from "Die Hard",

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:57.630
Beatrix Kiddo from "Kill
Bill", and Black Panther.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:59.430
- I'm gonna say Adonis
Creed right off the bat.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:00.880
Wonder Woman and Katniss, they're awesome,

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:03.620
and Beatrix, they're all
fighting ladies, but like-

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.710
- Yes, we all want
Michael B. Jordan, Mary.

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:08.560
We know, it's okay.
- I'll be honest about it.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.270
- I want to say Black Panther.

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:11.387
- I was about to say,

00:03:11.387 --> 00:03:12.550
I think I would go with Black Panther too.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:14.040
- I'm going with Beatrix from "Kill Bill".

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:15.920
I just watched that movie again,

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.100
and when she takes out the 88,

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:20.170
the Crazy 88s or whatever it
is, that's an insane scene.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.460
I would want her on my side.

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:22.293
- [Xolo] All right, let's see,

00:03:22.293 --> 00:03:24.860
how would you spend
your ideal Friday night?

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:26.370
At a party with my friends,

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:28.370
date night with my significant other,

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:32.340
inviting my closest friends
over to have a 'chill' night in.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:35.450
Heh, kind of a weird...
- Weird vibes.

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.810
- [Xolo] Having a nice
homemade dinner with my family,

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:40.700
practicing because there
are no days off, duh,

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.910
or by myself watching
my favorite TV series.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:43.743
- I'm not gonna lie,

00:03:43.743 --> 00:03:45.910
I read the "having a nice homemade dinner"

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:49.534
as "having a nice homicide"
(Jacob laughing)

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:52.310
I was like, a nice homicide
with my family? Okay!

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:55.290
- I think even with the weird tilde

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:56.270
that was entered in there,

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:57.740
I think inviting my closest friends over

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:59.110
to have a chill night
in is something that,

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:00.250
definitely during quarantine,

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.020
that I'm doing more than anything.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:04.460
- I'm gonna go with the same.
- Imma say date night.

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:06.990
- Date night with your significant other.

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:08.890
- I'm doing the closest friends.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:10.570
I just think that's the most realistic.

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:12.480
- Pick an 80s movie to reboot:

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.740
The Breakfast Club, Beverly
Hills Cop, Back to the Future,

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:18.380
Heathers, Do the Right
Thing, or The Goonies.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:20.560
I feel like Heather's kind of got a reboot

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.970
in the sense of the musical,

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:23.870
so I feel like I'm gonna
stick with The Breakfast Club.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:25.730
- I'm gonna have to go
with Heathers for sure.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:26.810
I love that movie.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:27.643
- Beverly Hills Cop.

00:04:27.643 --> 00:04:28.820
I really love that movie.
- Yeah,

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:31.090
I'm deciding between Beverly
Hills Cop and The Goonies.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:33.060
I feel like The Goonies deserves it more.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:34.700
- That's a weird way to phrase that.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:37.270
- You just don't deserve it!

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:38.103
- [Peyton] Finally,

00:04:38.103 --> 00:04:40.280
choose something important from Cobra Kai:

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:41.630
Hawk's tattoo,

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:43.400
All-Valley Karate Tournament,

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:45.010
Miguel's skeleton costume,

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:48.010
Mr. Miyagi's Medal of Honor, bonsai trees,

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.890
or Johnny's Coors banquet.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.810
- I think for me, it's
Johnny's Coors banquet.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:55.840
I think if there's anything
more synonymous with the show,

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.480
it's Johnny and his beer.
- I agree.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.450
- As much as wanna say Hawk's tattoo,

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:02.220
I gotta do Johnny's beer.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:03.177
It's the show, you know?

00:05:03.177 --> 00:05:04.620
- You guys are a bunch of Cobra Kais.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.130
I'm thinking Miyagi's medal
of honor, because technically,

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:10.700
that's the thing that started
the whole season two fight.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.510
If you go far enough back

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:13.343
- Well I mean,

00:05:13.343 --> 00:05:15.600
technically what started
the fight is your inability

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.060
to walk down a hill without
having to hold someone's hand.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:21.448
But I mean-
(Jacob and Mary laugh)

00:05:21.448 --> 00:05:23.340
(cool rock music)

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.961
Cobra Kai runs through my veins!

00:05:24.961 --> 00:05:27.240
- Cobra Kai!
- Me too!

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:30.200
- What about you Mary?
- 100% Miyagi-Do

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.033
- I can't think

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:34.480
of anything I'd rather be
100% of than Cobra Kai.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.600
- Cobra Kai runs through my veins.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:40.130
You're smart, determined, and
stronger than all Miyagi-Dos.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:41.680
- Please tell me that's not
actually what's written.

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:42.513
- That's really what's written.

00:05:42.513 --> 00:05:44.640
- It says you're stronger
than all the Miyagi-Dos?

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:45.640
- (group) Yes!
- That's so

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.010
a Cobra Kai something to say.

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:48.710
You're 100% Miyagi-Do.

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:50.700
You're brave, level-headed, and resilient.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.230
You're very in tune with your emotions

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:54.320
because they're usually
what motivate your actions.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.490
- I think there was
never a doubt in my mind.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:58.820
- I was questioning Peyton.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:02.000
Cause I feel like knowing
Peyton in real life

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.870
you're such a nice person.

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:06.440
I was not expecting the
more cutthroat answers.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:07.730
- Nah, she's pretty mean.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:08.890
- We bonded last season,

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:11.320
and we went out and we had a lot of fun.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:14.388
So she knows me well now
(Mary laughs)

00:06:14.388 --> 00:06:16.066
- Apparently not well enough.

00:06:16.066 --> 00:06:18.899
(cool rock music)

